d-springtail` is closed, so the narrow hosted-OpenAI removal is now eligible.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete the scheduled aliases and require their canonical forms: reason-bearing `force=\"<reason>\"` and hosted `openai-responses:<model>`. Preserve custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints on Chat Completions; they are not the hosted surface being removed. Update release material, generated references, schemas, examples, and tests as a deliberate pre-1.0 break.\n\n## Scope\n\n- deprecation registry and transition/provider parsing\n- CLI/Python/MCP schemas and documentation/examples\n- changelog/release notes and focused compatibility tests\n\n## Testing\n\nCover each removed spelling failing at its public boundary, canonical replacements succeeding, and a custom endpoint still using Chat Completions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `force_close=` and boolean `force=True` are rejected; `force=\"<explicit reason>\"` remains accepted.\n- [ ] Hosted `openai-chat:` selection is rejected; hosted `openai-responses:` works.\n- [ ] Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints retain their Chat Completions dialect.\n- [ ] Changelog, release notes, schemas, generated references, examples, and tests record the breaking replacements.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"remove scheduled deprecation registry entries"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"remove force_close/boolean-force compatibility paths"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/providers.py","reason":"remove hosted openai-chat compatibility selection"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"update public MCP transition contract"},{"path":"docs","reason":"update maintained compatibility and provider guidance"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"record pre-1.0 breaking removals"},{"path":"tests","reason":"prove removed and canonical public behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impa